infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Bigger pool vs guaranteeing the return
  desc A leak drains any pool at its own rate — only the structural fix stops the bleeding
  compares
    - label Bigger pool: the reflex fix
      children
        - label Leak drains any pool at its own rate
          desc A leak is a rate, not a fixed cost — every pool still empties
        - label Outage delayed, not prevented
          desc Only turns a 3-hour outage into a 6-hour one
        - label Hides the cause past the deploy
          desc Symptom surfaces hours later, looking like random overload
    - label Guarantee the return: try/finally
      children
        - label release() runs on success and on throw
          desc Or using, defer, a context manager, a scoped transaction
        - label Bounds the cause, not the symptom
          desc Stops the leak instead of inflating the buffer that delays it
        - label Leak detection points to the branch
          desc leakDetectionThreshold ~2s emits a stack trace of the borrow
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
